extends RefCounted
## Version 5 help text (STE), one source for the How to play "People" tab and the Codex "People" tab.
## [id, title, icon, codex category, text]. Keep each sentence short: one instruction or one fact.

const CATEGORIES := ["Interface", "Society", "People", "Structures", "World"]

const TOPICS := [
	["dock", "The left dock and messages", "dock", "Interface",
		"Everything the game tells you by itself goes to the left: an urgent line, new messages and the dock. The dock has tabs: Goals, Alerts, Events, Traffic, Requests and News. A number on a tab counts its items; its colour shows the most urgent one. Each card can be minimised, pinned or closed. The dock can be minimised, pinned or closed; key L opens and closes it. A pinned dock stays open when a window covers it. The middle of the view stays free. Settings, Notifications: for each kind of message choose Pop up, Badge only or Off."],
	["build", "The build bar", "build", "Interface",
		"The build bar at the bottom has the tabs Life, Food, Habitat, Industry, Power, Logistics, Science and Civic. A tab opens a strip of cards above it. The strip stays low, so the middle of the view stays free. The mouse wheel moves the strip sideways. Pick a card: the strip folds to the tabs, and a small panel at the bottom shows the cost, the size, the keys and why you cannot place there. Left click places the structure. The strip comes back after one placement, or when you press Esc or the right mouse button. Shift and click keeps the tool, and the strip stays folded. Remove asks you in the same small panel."],
	["roofs", "Roofs off", "roof_off", "Interface",
		"Key Y or the roof button on the right takes every roof and upper wall away, so you see into every building at once. Press it again to put the roofs back. The game keeps your choice. In the over-the-shoulder view the roofs always stay on, and the button waits."],
	["floors", "Floor selector", "overlay", "Interface",
		"Select a structure with more than one floor. A strip on the right shows one button for each floor and All. A floor button cuts the building away above that floor, so you see inside. All shows the whole building. PgUp and PgDn step one floor. In the over-the-shoulder view, the view follows the floor of the person."],
	["settings", "Settings and keys", "settings", "Interface",
		"Open Settings from the menu (Esc). Changes apply at once and stay on this device. Quality: Low, Medium, High or Ultra. Interface scale: 80 to 140 %; every window stays inside the view. Glass blur, cheeky dialogue, screen-edge pan, camera speed and camera shake. Five volume sliders. Notifications: Pop up, Badge only or Off for each kind of message. The Keys card lists every key and mouse control. F1 opens How to play."],
	["sound_in", "Sound and weather indoors", "volume", "Interface",
		"Inside a room, a corridor or the dome, the wind and storm sounds drop to a faint, low rumble and the room tone takes over. The change takes half a second. Outside you hear the full weather. In the over-the-shoulder view no weather comes inside, and the sound rule for indoors always applies."],
	["follow", "Over the shoulder", "follow", "Society",
		"Select a person and press V. The camera goes behind them. Mouse wheel: zoom, from a face close-up to 8 m. Right drag: go round the person in a full circle, and tilt the camera from near the floor to high above. Middle drag, or Alt and right drag: look round while the camera stays. Q and E: the other shoulder. R: back behind the person. While the person walks, the camera goes back by itself after 4 seconds without input. Tab: the next person. Esc or V: back to the colony. The roofs stay on and no weather comes in. The card at the top left shows their mood, needs, what they do and what they said. Switch follows the person they talk to. The rest of the interface goes dim."],
	["bubbles", "Speech bubbles", "people", "Society",
		"People talk at meals, at work and in leisure places. A bubble shows the name and the line. What they say comes from their mood, their friends and what happened today. In the follow view you see the bubbles of the people near you. The personnel file keeps the last lines."],
	["rag", "The Regolith Rag", "newspaper", "Society",
		"The colony tabloid (key J). A new issue comes out each morning. It prints gossip about couples, feuds and scandals from what really happened. Click a name: the camera goes to that person and their file opens. The Serious news strip at the foot lists the real problems. The header lists the back issues."],
	["unrest", "Unrest", "people", "Society",
		"Unrest is 0 to 100 for each base. It comes from low satisfaction, bad attitudes, punishments, homes below the rank, deaths and ration cuts. Grumbling from 25. Slowdown from 40: work is 15 % slower. Protest from 55: a group gathers at the dome plaza or the biggest leisure room and shouts its demand. Strike from 70: a department stops work. Riot from 85: fights, damage and break-ins. The top bar shows the stage; a banner shows from Protest up."],
	["responses", "Answering unrest", "sev_warning", "Society",
		"The banner has 7 answers. Each shows its effect and its cost. Meet the demand, a leisure day or a party lower unrest; they cost stock or a day of work. Amnesty frees prisoners. Replace the captain of the angry department. Arrest the ringleaders: unrest falls only when people think it is fair. Lock down: see Lockdown. An answer used recently must wait."],
	["lockdown", "Lockdown", "lock", "Society",
		"Lock down is one answer to unrest. The doors of the base close for 2 game hours. People stay in their rooms, so a riot cannot spread. There is no leisure, and unrest rises a little. The banner says LOCKDOWN and counts the time until the doors open. You can also start it in the Crew window (key U), Security tab, with Lock down this base."],
	["security", "Security and fights", "shelter", "Society",
		"Security officers patrol public places. They stop fights and arrest the person who started it. Aim for 1 officer for each 12 people. A security office gives them a post and a faster response. Fights come from enemies, from very bad attitudes and from riots, and fighters get hurt. In a riot, people damage rooms and take goods. Open the Crew window (key U), Security tab: it shows the officers against the target, the jail cells in use, the fights now (Show moves the camera) and the prisoners. Change a job there: a security officer needs security skill 40 or more."],
	["jail", "The jail", "lock", "Society",
		"A jail has 2, 4 or 8 cells (size S, M or L; research Civic Planning). An officer walks the arrested person to a free cell. The prisoner wears prison clothes, eats, drinks and sleeps in the cell, and does not work. When the time is up, the prisoner goes free and a message tells you. Without a jail, an arrested person stays in their quarters, which is weaker. The discipline order Jail confines the person to their quarters when no jail works. Amnesty frees every prisoner at once."],
	["love", "Couples and break-ups", "heart", "Society",
		"People who talk often become friends, or rivals and enemies. Two people who like each other start dating. After some days they become partners, and partners can marry. A wedding makes the whole colony happier for a day. A couple that stops getting on breaks up: both are unhappy for 2 days. An affair can come out; then the cheated partner breaks up. A colonist can fall for a visitor (a fling). A toast tells you each of these moments. The Rag prints them."],
	["requests", "Requests from people", "heart", "Society",
		"A colonist in love with a visitor can ask to leave the colony on the visitor's ship. A card in the Requests tab of the dock asks you. Let them go: they leave for good, with their skills. You confirm first. Refuse: they stay, but their satisfaction and attitude fall for 3 days. File opens their personnel file. Show moves the camera to them. The request stays until you answer; the card says what happens if nobody does."],
	["tourism", "Tourism", "credits", "Society",
		"A tourist liner brings tourists. In the Traffic tab you grant or deny the landing. A tourist eats, sleeps, shops and visits venues, and pays credits for each visit. A tourist with no bed pays 20 % less; the Traffic tab says so. Tourists never raise colony alerts. The Tourism card in the Colony window (key C), People tab, shows the visitors now, the credits earned and the balance. Credits buy goods from traders."],
	["secrets", "Secrets", "sparkle", "Society",
		"The colony hides a few secrets. Look for them. A hidden medal shows in the Awards only after you find it. The Codex lists a secret once you have found it."],
	["chat", "Idle talk", "people", "Society",
		"A person with nothing to do looks for another idle person nearby in the same room, walks over and starts a talk. The topic comes from how they know each other: small talk, gossip, a moan about work, a joke, a rivalry or a flirt. Two adults who like each other flirt. When the chemistry is strong, they tease with cheeky lines. This never happens with children. A person who is not interested makes it awkward, and that is a small drama. Settings, Cheeky dialogue: Off gives mild flirting only. In the over-the-shoulder view, the bubbles show the lines."],
	["parties", "Celebrations and parties", "music", "Society",
		"A birthday, a promotion, a goal, a medal, a new structure, a wedding, an adoption or a record is a reason for a party. A card in the Requests tab asks you: choose the place and the hours (1 to 3; one party hour is 60 seconds), then Throw the party or Skip it. A party uses 1 unit of drinks, snacks or rations for every 2 guests. If nobody answers in 5 minutes, friends gather by themselves, without drinks. Guests dance, talk and toast; friends come first. Satisfaction and friendships rise. Small drama happens at most parties. Big drama happens now and then: a public break-up, a jealous scene, an affair that comes out, a proposal or a fight. Security answers a fight. The Events tab shows the parties now (Show, Follow a guest). The News tab lists the messages. The Rag reports it next morning. To throw a party by yourself, select a cantina, a lounge, a park or the super dome and open the Party tab."],
	["hr", "The HR office", "colonists", "People",
		"The HR office lets people complain and ask for a transfer. Build it in the Civic tab (research Civic Planning). Size S has 1 post, M 2 and L 3. Make a person an HR officer in the Crew window (key U): Change a job. The office needs power and a staffed desk. Only then can a person with satisfaction under 45, or a grievance, walk to the office and file a complaint. Being heard gives a small rise in satisfaction. HR solves about 2 of 3 complaints by itself in a day. The others wait for you. Every 3 days HR runs a staff survey: satisfaction by department, the top 3 complaints and the morale trend. Without an active HR office, none of this happens, and unhappy people only grumble."],
	["complaints", "Complaints and transfers", "orders", "People",
		"A complaint waits in the Requests tab and in the Crew window, HR tab. Each option shows its effect before you choose: mediate a feud, move the person's home, change their job, give a leisure day, leave it to HR, or dismiss. A complaint that nobody answers for 3 days is dismissed. A very unhappy person (satisfaction under 25) can ask HR for a transfer off world. Approve: they leave on the next ship that has seats, and the colony loses them. You confirm first. Refuse: their satisfaction and attitude fall, and the request can come back. Many refusals raise unrest. A transfer request that nobody answers for 2 days lapses."],
	["hr_officer", "Loved in public, gossiped about in private", "heart", "People",
		"People are warm to the HR officer's face and talk about them behind their back. The officer has two values. In public: 0 to 100, what people say to the officer. In private: -100 to 100, what they say when the officer is away. The HR tab in the Crew window shows both. The Rag prints HR gossip in its gossip column."],
	["file", "Personnel file", "colonists", "People",
		"One person (the File button, or the Follow card). File: rank, role, home, traits, skills, satisfaction and attitude with their reasons. Social: friends, partner, rivals and enemies. A secret crush does not show. Review: write a review, or reward or punish the person. History (File tab): the effects on the person now, with the time left, and what happened to them, newest first."],
	["discipline", "Reviews and discipline", "orders", "People",
		"Rewards (praise, bonus leisure, a gift) raise satisfaction; rivals feel small envy. Punishments (warning, extra shift, ration cut, confinement, demotion, jail) improve attitude now and lower satisfaction. Friends see every punishment. When the person did nothing wrong, the punishment is unfair: fairness falls and unrest rises. Every order shows its effect on the person and on others first. Then you confirm."],
	["families", "Families and children", "home", "People",
		"Partners move in together when a unit has room. When no unit is free, a card asks you: Try again after you build a home, or Keep them apart (both are unhappy for 3 days). Partners and married couples can adopt a child: open the personnel file, Social tab, Adopt a child. It needs a medical bay and a free bunk in their home. A child goes to school at the academy, plays in parks and never works. A child grows up after some days and takes the job of their best school subject."],
	["ranks", "Ranks and departments", "people", "People",
		"Each base has a Base Commander. Each department (Industry, Science, Food, Maintenance, Security) has a Captain and up to 2 First Hands. The others are Specialists, Crew or Trainees by skill. Leaders make their department faster. Open the Crew window (key U) and drag a person onto a rank. A star marks the simulation's choice. A rank expects a home: the commander and the captains an executive unit."],
	["priorities", "Job priorities", "orders", "People",
		"Open the Colonists window (key P), Priorities tab. Each row is one colonist. Each column is one kind of work: construction, food, industry, logistics and repair. A cell shows 3 First, 2 Normal, 1 Last or Never. Click a cell to step to the next value. The top row, Colony default (gold), is the value of every colonist who has no own value. A cell with a cyan frame is the own value of that colonist; it overrides the colony default. A dim cell follows the colony default. Reset removes the own values of one colonist. Thirst, hunger, exhaustion and your orders come before all work."],
	["skills", "Skills", "research", "People",
		"11 skills, 0 to 100, shown as levels 1 to 5: Novice, Trained, Skilled, Expert, Master. A Novice works at x0.7, a Master at x1.4, with fewer mistakes. Skills grow with work and at the academy. A skill not used for a long time falls a little."],
	["academy", "The academy", "research", "People",
		"A course teaches one skill one level up. The student walks to the academy and learns only while they sit in class. A teacher needs 60 or more in that skill and doubles the pace. Without a teacher, the instructor console teaches up to level 3. Enrol a person in the Crew window, Academy tab. The table there shows every level of the crew."],
	["housing", "Homes", "home", "People",
		"Home quality: dorm 1, family unit 2, executive unit 3, penthouse 4. A person whose home is below what their rank expects is less satisfied. Partners share a unit; a family needs a family unit. The Crew window, Housing tab, shows every home and who waits for a better one. Drag a person onto a unit to move them."],
	["giants", "New structures", "cat_civic", "Structures",
		"Residence tube (M to XL): family units, or executive units after the research Civic Planning. Apartment block (size XXL): 3 floors, a lift, 10 family units and 2 penthouses; research High-rise Housing. Retail shop and park: leisure places. Academy: courses. Security office: officers patrol and stop fights. Jail: 2, 4 or 8 cells. Distillery: drinks and snacks. HR office: complaints, transfers and staff surveys. Super dome (size XXXXL): see The super dome. XXL and XXXXL are one giant size each. The Civic tab of the build bar has the security office, the jail and the super dome."],
	["venues", "Venues and goods", "cat_civic", "Structures",
		"A retail shop, a park and the super dome hold venues: shops, a bar, a cafe, a gym, the club and more. Select the structure and open the Venues tab. A venue is open when it has power, its staff are at work and, for a shop, goods in stock. The simulation proposes the staff; you can choose a person for each job. Carriers bring the goods (luxury goods, clothing, snacks, drinks, gadgets, gifts) from storage. The distillery, workshop, electronics fab and fabricator make them; traders sell them. Colonists use venues for free; a good venue raises their satisfaction. Tourists pay credits for each visit."],
	["dome", "The super dome", "cat_civic", "Structures",
		"Research Arcology unlocks it. It needs graphene and metamaterials, and much power, water and air. It is built in 9 stages: foundation, levels 1 to 5, the dome frame, the dome glass and the fit-out. Select it while it grows: a badge shows STAGE n OF 9. When it is finished, shops and businesses stand on levels 1 and 2 round an open atrium with a pool and a park, 16 venues in all, and 30 homes above. Venues need staff and goods. Tourists pay to visit. Use the floor selector to look into each level."],
	["planets", "Planets differ", "planet", "World",
		"Dry world: warm dust, good sun, light wind. Dust storms, wind storms and dust devils come. Cold world: short days (300 s) and weak sun (0.6 times). Wind turbines carry the night. Dust storms and dust devils come less often. Airless world: strong sun (1.2 times), no wind and double radiation. No dust storms, wind storms or dust devils come, but meteors come 1.4 times as often, and solar flares 1.5 times as often and stronger. A wind turbine and an atmosphere processor need air: on the airless world the game refuses them and says why. The forecast and the Codex, Hazard tab, list only the hazards of your planet."],
]

## Topic by id ({} when unknown).
static func topic(id: String) -> Array:
	for t in TOPICS:
		if String(t[0]) == id:
			return t
	return []
